## Quick Start (5 Minutes)

### Run Korame Locally

```bash
# 1. Clone repository
git clone <korame-repo>
cd korame

# 2. Start Docker services
docker-compose up -d

# 3. Verify it's running
curl http://localhost:8000/health

# 4. Create a test story
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/artifacts \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer test-token" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "type": "UserStory",
    "title": "Implement JWT validation",
    "description": "As a developer, I want JWT tokens validated...",
    "acceptance_criteria": ["Validates signature", "Checks expiration"]
  }'

# 5. Watch the state transitions
curl http://localhost:8000/api/v1/artifacts/story-123/state \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer test-token"
```

### Architecture in 30 Seconds

```
User creates requirement
         ↓ (RTE Agent)
Design created
         ↓ (Architect Agent)
Code generated
         ↓ (Developer Agent)
Code reviewed ← GATE: If fails, loops back to Developer
         ↓
Security scanned ← GATE: If fails, loops back to Developer
         ↓
Tests generated & run ← GATE: If coverage < 80%, loops back
         ↓
Business accepts ← GATE: If fails, full loop back to Developer
         ↓
Deployed to production
         ↓
Complete ✓
```

**Key:** No gate can be skipped. All gates must pass before moving forward.

